    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0477" n="1063" xml:id="pg1063"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Korea/7–1949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Muccio</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-19T14:00:00+10:00">July 19, 1949—2 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>884. ReEmbtel 881, July 18. Following arrest Choi Yung Sik Saturday, four other
                    newspaper reporters arrested later same day: Lee Moon Nam, reporter <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Korea Press</hi>; Pak In Hwan, reporter <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cha Too Shin Moon;</hi> Sam Rai Sup, reporter <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Koo Kto Shin Moon;</hi> Huh Moon Taek, reporter <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cho Sun Chong Ang Daily</hi>. All five arrested assigned
                    cover UNCOK press conferences and presumed to have prepared Communist-slanted
                    questionnaire handed UNCOK delegate Singh July 14, copy of which being air
                        pouched.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d272-f1"/> Lee Ho, Director National Police,
                    informed AP correspondent today all five have since confessed membership SKLP,
                    Communist underground organization South Korea. Arrested men held incommunicado
                    since arrest despite requests US reporters and UNCOK secretariat see arrested
                    men.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d272-f1" n="1" xml:id="d272-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted with despatch No. 440, July 22, from Seoul; not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
